Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["A Note on the \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Glass Box\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
Approach", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.97688929871796*^9, 3.976889556697713*^9, 
  3.976889851295733*^9},ExpressionUUID->"5c85bee8-6fff-4c6e-ba13-\
21ee29fd942b"],

Cell["\<\
In developing this toolkit, we made a conscious decision to implement the \
engine for the time being as a Script rather than a compiled Package.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.97688929871796*^9, {3.976889563666814*^9, 
   3.9768895935975227`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3ad9d1db-a459-453c-8a0f-\
ab0ff2d3dcce"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In professional Wolfram Language development, it is standard practice to \
encapsulate code in strict Packages ",
 StyleBox["(BeginPackage[...])", "Input"],
 ", hiding the internal machinery in a private namespace. While this ensures \
safety for commercial libraries, it creates a \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Black \
Box\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] that is antithetical to our present pedagogical \
goals and to the current prototypical status of the code."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.97688929871796*^9, {3.976889563666814*^9, 
   3.976889649088426*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"4dc06e3b-c26f-4db0-9f58-\
2dfe4bc9350a"],

Cell["With a Glass Box, the reader can:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.97688929871796*^9, {3.976889563666814*^9, 
   3.9768896868815203`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"33d29148-4fb9-4c6d-b1a1-\
1cb356be3429"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Inspect the machinery: Type ",
 StyleBox["?valence", "Input"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["?metricRules", "Input"],
 " and immediately see the physics logic, not an opaque symbol."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.97688929871796*^9, {3.976889563666814*^9, 
   3.976889704406357*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"65f78dce-8047-4c0d-b6fa-\
568aac671db2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Modify the engine: Experiment with new rules (e.g., ",
 StyleBox["torsion", "Input"],
 ") without fighting a locked namespace."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.97688929871796*^9, {3.976889563666814*^9, 
   3.97688971686047*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ae8a7d07-2d40-4606-a995-\
827006906cad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Trust the derivation: Verify that the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "be2a8e0b-7f8c-4cab-989e-aeee3f8082e1"],
 "\:200b on the screen is the same mathematical object as in the code, with \
no hidden translation layer."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.97688929871796*^9, {3.976889563666814*^9, 
   3.976889758341415*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d65a00ca-c878-477e-af3e-\
c3a97e6d08ae"],

Cell["\<\
Therefore, we load RelativityToolkit directly into the \
user\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Global notebook context, prioritizing transparency \
over isolation at this stage of development.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.97688929871796*^9, {3.976889563666814*^9, 3.976889759548066*^9}, {
   3.976889789792459*^9, 
   3.9768898423425837`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1268bb70-e6fd-453d-aa58-\
a609a84f0acd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A side-effect of this choice is that we may overwrite some System symbols. \
For instance, we\[CloseCurlyQuote]re giving up the Euler Gamma Function with \
symbol ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[CapitalGamma]", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "b370777c-cada-4ea5-8171-eab410dd1406"],
 " in favor of the same symbol for the Christoffel symbols. "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976890630834564*^9, 
  3.976890700972865*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d8ec265a-4f93-425e-b1c0-\
cd7b12fd4800"],

